      "problem": "Which of the following equations have no real solution?\n\nI. $\\sqrt{2x-3}=1$\n\nII. $\\sqrt{4x+1}=-6$\n\nIII. $\\sqrt{2x-1}=12$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that a square root is always positive or zero. So, a radical equation has no real solution if it states that a square root is equal to a negative number.\n\nOf the given equations, only II states that a square root is equal to a negative number. Therefore, equation II has no real solution.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
